ref=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/56330/shonn-miller\">Shonn Miller</a> added 14, including the last eight of the game, and UConn closed on a 16-3 run to defeat Houston 69-57 on Sunday.\n\nGibbs started the run with back-to-back 3-pointers for a 59-54 lead with 5:21 left. After a Houston free throw at 4:14, Gibbs made two free throws and he answered a Cougars basket by feeding Miller for a dunk with 2:07 remaining. Miller also scored the final three baskets after two Houston misses and a turnover.\n\n<a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/3147351/daniel-hamilton\">Daniel Hamilton</a> also had 14 points for the Huskies (12-5, 3-2 American) and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/player/_/id/3934622/jalen-adams\">Jalen Adams</a> had 13.\n\nRob Gray Jr. led Houston (13-4, 3-2) with 15 in the low-scoring game between teams averaging 80.8 (Cougars) and 76.8 points.\n\nHouston led 35-28 at the half as Gray scored 12 points but Gibbs and Miller combined for 25 in the second half when UConn shot 48 percent and made 11 of 12 free throws.","images":[]},"videos":[],"news":[],"source":{"summary":true,"boxscore":"full","playByPlay":"full"}}